# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC and every committed file is world-readable,
# both on github.com and (for /public and /content) as a live URL
# on sohamdange.github.io. Ignoring a file here only prevents
# FUTURE commits — it does not remove anything already in history.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/

# TypeScript incremental build cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment files
.env
.env*.local
.env.production

# Credentials and keys — never publish
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
id_rsa*
*.credentials.json
serviceAccount*.json

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# Staging area for anything NOT meant to be published.
# Drop drafts, resumes, scans, client work, or reference files here —
# nothing in this folder can be committed or deployed by accident.
/private/

# Personal documents — resumes, transcripts, scans, letters.
# A PDF in /public is fetchable at a guessable URL even if no page
# links to it. Use `git add -f <file>` to publish one deliberately.
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx

# Archives — usually an accidental drag-and-drop, not site content
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# CAD, simulation, and analysis artifacts.
# Often large, and often covered by employer/university IP terms.
# Publish a specific one with `git add -f <file>`.
*.step
*.stp
*.iges
*.igs
*.sldprt
*.sldasm
*.slddrw
*.catpart
*.catproduct
*.prt
*.ipt
*.iam
*.f3d
*.dwg
*.dxf
*.cdb
*.db
*.rst
*.rth
*.f06
*.odb
*.inp
*.cas
*.dat.gz

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code — local machine settings only.
# .claude/settings.json (shared config) stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local git hooks — kept out of the repo deliberately.
# The pre-commit publishing gate lives here on this machine only;
# it is not distributed with a clone. See CLAUDE.md.
.githooks/

# Working backlog — local only, not for the public repo.
TASKS.md
